module test.claim.fleet.machine_lifecycle_witness

// WITNESS: THE LIFECYCLE TRANSITIONS OF A FLEET MACHINE (gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_authority P13; 2.5, O4).
//
// WHAT IS ALREADY GUARANTEED ELSEWHERE (the claim does NOT re-establish): A2's fold and its refusals are
// witnessed in test.claim.fleet.fleet_machine_unit_binding_witness, the registry's two-axis admission in
// test.claim.hostname_allocation_witness, and the enrollment admission in test.claim.fleet.fleet_enrollment_
// witness. This file claims only P13's own three acceptance bullets and its Done condition -- that every O4
// transition has a modeled route and none is a hand step -- and it claims them by RUNNING the producers
// named inside the model, not by reading the model's text. A transition that refuses nothing, or a route
// whose legs name nothing, is exactly the failure mode this file exists to red.
//
// THE FIXTURES, DECLARED (DESIGN: "a witness that supplies values at its boundary declares them and owes an
// inhabitance claim on the real producer path"). The machine is the one the fleet has fully observed:
// mtcollins1 holds a registry row (with a drawn pending name, so the rename route has a real promotion to
// consume), an admitted enrollment with a RAM-image backing, and an A2 binding whose unit key is its real
// observed serial. The replacement board is a fixture serial -- it exists to be a DIFFERENT board, and no
// live machine is rebound to it or retired below.
//
// RUN ATTESTING THESE CLAIMS (the receipt cited in the PR; the required v2-bootstrap job evaluates no
// witness outside its two emitted closures, so the witness is executed directly, with BOTH source roots):
//   gunbc run --claim-run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 \
//     --entry dag/test/claim/fleet/machine_lifecycle_witness.dag

